# Keyword reference from the user (Keywords 4_14_22 doc). Evergreen and expansion keywords are merged into kind=keyword (evergreen distinction ignored, user 2026-10-22). Summaries are the doc's plain-language wording (first two points), not rules text: a few are inexact (e.g. Bolster, Renown, Fabricate); check Forge script / Oracle text before relying on one. ability_word entries (Landfall, Raid...) are flavour labels, not Forge K: keywords.
keywords[172]{name,kind,example,summary}:
  Deathtouch,keyword,Sedge Scorpion,"Whenever a creature with deathtouch deals damage to another creature, that creature will die. It does not have to be combat damage, so if you have a card like Rabid Bite, it will still kill the creature dealt damage."
  Defender,keyword,Wall of Mist,"Creature cannot attack. In the past, there was a rule that said \"Walls can't attack.\" So if you see an old creature with the type \"Wall\", but it doesn't have defender in the text-box, it still has defender."
  Double Strike,keyword,Boros Swiftblade,Creature deals both first strike damage and regular damage.
  Enchant,keyword,Abundant Growth,"Written as \"Enchant X\" where X is a permanent type These are auras."
  Equip,keyword,Sword of Feast and Famine,"Written as \"Equip X\" where X is a mana cost These are equipment."
  First Strike,keyword,Battle Hurda,"Creature with first strike deals damage before creatures without first strike in combat. For example, if you have a 2/2 elf and a 2/2 soldier with first strike in combat, the elf would die before it deals damage to the soldier."
  Flash,keyword,Bounding Krasis,"This is on nonland permanent cards (creatures, artifact, enchantments, planeswalkers). Permits you to cast those spells whenever you could cast an instant."
  Flying,keyword,Storm Crow,Creatures with flying can only be blocked by other creatures with flying or by creatures with reach.
  Haste,keyword,Tenement Crasher,"Creatures with haste may attack or activate \"tap\" abilities the turn they come into play, i.e. no summoning sickness."
  Lifelink,keyword,Bishop's Soldier,"Whenever a creature with lifelink deals damage, either to an opponent or creature, you gain life equal to the amount of damage. All damage happens at the same time. If you are dealt lethal damage, but have a lifelink creature to block that brings you back up a"
  Menace,keyword,Ruin Grinder,"Creatures with menace can only be blocked by 2 or more creatures. When paired with deathtouch, it's very potent."
  Protection,keyword,Apostle of Purifying Light,"Written as \"Protection from X\" This is complicated."
  Prowess,keyword,Monastery Swiftspear,"Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, prowess creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn. Does stack, so if you cast 2 noncreature spells, prowess creatures get +1/+1 for each of those spells, getting +2/+2 total."
  Reach,keyword,Giant Spider,Creatures with reach may block creatures with flying.
  Trample,keyword,Colossal Dreadmaw,Creatures with trample deal excess damage to defending player. Example
  Vigilance,keyword,Serra Angel,Attacking does not cause creature to tap.
  Ward,keyword,Dreadlight Monstrosity,"Written as \"Ward [cost]\" If a creature with ward becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell unless the opponent pays the ward cost."
  Attach,action,"","Used on auras, equipment, and fortifications (only one fortification, Darksteel Garrison, in the game.) Used to \"put on\" an aura or equipment to a permanent."
  Clash,action,Fire Juggler,"When a spell tells players to clash, each player reveals the top card of their library. When they do, the person with the higher mana value of the revealed card wins the clash. In the event of a tie, there is no winner."
  Counter,action,Counterspell,"Countering a spell or ability removes it from the stack. Also called permission, because you get to say \"no\" to so many things."
  Reconfigure,action,The Reality Chip,"Written as \"Reconfigure X\" where X is a mana cost These are artifact creatures that are also equipment."
  Regeneration,action,Ancient Silverback,"Written as \"regenerate: [cost]\" When the regeneration cost is paid, it gives that permanent a \"regeneration shield\" for the rest of the turn."
  Sacrifice,action,Chainer's Edict,"The owner of a permanent places it into their own graveyard due to an effect or spell. Some spells cause you to sacrifice a creature as an additional cost, sometimes spells an opponent cast can cause you to sacrifice a creature."
  Scry,action,Crystal Ball,"Written as \"Scry X\" where X is a number Look at the top X cards of your library, put any number on the bottom of your library. Put the rest back in any order."
  Tap/untap,action,"",Allows you to tap or untap a permanent.
  Absorb,keyword,"","Only on one card: Lymph Sliver Written as \"Absorb X\" where X is a number"
  Adapt,keyword,Growth-Chamber Guardian,"Written as \"[cost] Adapt X\", where X is a number When the adapt cost is paid, put X +1/+1 counters on the creatures whose ability was activated."
  Adventure,keyword,Bonecrusher Giant,"On a card with adventure, you may cast a spell for it's adventure cost. If you do, exile that card. You may then cast the creature side from exile. You have to cast adventure spell, then creature half. You cannot cast creature half, then adventure from exile."
  Affinity,keyword,Thoughtcast,"Written as \"Affinity for X\", where X is a card type Most commonly written as \"affinity for artifacts\", a card can have affinity for anything."
  Afterlife,keyword,Orzhov Enforcer,"Written as \"Afterlife X\", where X is an number When a creature with afterlife dies, it's controller creates X 1/1 black and white spirit tokens with flying equal to the afterlife number."
  Aftermath,keyword,Commit to Memory,"Only on split cards One side may only be cast from your hand, the other side may only be cast from the graveyard."
  Alliance,keyword,Gala Greeters,"Basically \"Landfall\", but on creatures. Whenever another creature enters, some effect happens."
  Amplify,keyword,Kilnmouth Dragon,"Written as \"Amplify X\", where X is a number When you cast a card with amplify, you may reveal any number of cards that share a card type with that card. The card that was cast then enters with a number of +1/+1 counters equal to X times the amount of cards rev"
  Annihilator,keyword,Ulamog's Crusher,"Written as \"Annihilator X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with annihilator attacks, the defending player sacrifices X permanents, where X is the number associated with annihilator."
  Aura Swap,keyword,Arcanum Wings,"Written as \"Aura Swap X\", where X is a mana cost When a card with aura swap is attached to a creature, you may pay the cost associated with aura swap to return the attached card to your hand and attach an aura from your hand to the same creature."
  Banding,keyword,Knights of Thorn,"Historically, THE MOST complicated mechanic in all of MTG history. 53 words of rules text:"
  Battle Cry,keyword,Signal Pest,"Whenever a creature with battle cry attacks, other attacking creatures get +1/+0 until the end of turn."
  Bestow,keyword,Celestial Archon,"Written as \"Bestow [cost]\" When you pay the bestow cost, you use a creature with bestow as an aura for a creature on the battlefield. If the bestowed creature dies, the creature with bestow stays on the battlefield."
  Blitz,keyword,"","Written as \"Blitz [cost]\" You may cast a card for it's blitz cost. If you do, it gains haste. Sacrifice it at the next end step and draw a card."
  Bloodrush,keyword,Skarrg Goliath,"Written as \"Bloodrush [cost]\" You may discard a creature with bloodrush by paying its bloodrush cost. Then, a target creature is granted a boost and abilities based off the discarded creature."
  Bloodthirst,keyword,Scab-Clan Mauler,"Written as \"Bloodthirst X\", where X is a number Creatures with Bloodthirst counters enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them, if an opponent was dealt damage this turn."
  Bolster,keyword,"Dromoka, the Eternal","Written as \"Bolster X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with bolster attacks, you put X +1/+1 counters on target creature you control with the lowest toughness equal to the X in bolster."
  Bushido,keyword,Devoted Retainer,"Written as \"Bushido X\", where X is a number If a creature with Bushido is blocked or blocks, it gets +X/+X until the end of the turn, where X is the number associated with Bushido."
  Buyback,keyword,Capsize,"Written as \"Buyback X\", where X is a mana cost. Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a card, you may pay the buyback cost. If you do, instead of the card going to your graveyard, it goes back to your hand after resolving."
  Cascade,keyword,Bloodbraid Elf,"Whenever a you cast a card with cascade, exile the top card of your library until you find a card with a lesser converted mana cost, then you may cast that card without paying its mana cost. 2 spells for the cost of 1 spell. Very powerful, considered broken."
  Casualty,keyword,A Little Chat,"Written as \"Casualty X\", where X is a number When you cast a card with casualty, you may sacrifice a creature with power equal to the X value. If you do, copy the spell."
  Champion,keyword,Wanderwine Prophets,"Written as \"Champion a [creature type]\" When you cast a creature with champion, you must exile a card that is the type referred to in the champion keyword. If the champion card leaves play, the exiled card will be returned to the battlefield."
  Changeling,keyword,Chameleon Colossus,"Creatures with changeling count as all creature types, therefore benefitting from all bonuses associated with tribal synergies. Very common in decks without many good creatures of a specific type."
  Channel,keyword,Greater Tanuki,"Written as \"Channel [cost]\" You may pay the channel cost of a card in your hand, if you do, you discard that card and yield some effect."
  Cipher,keyword,Call of the Nightwing,"When you cast a spell with cipher, you may exile it as it resolves. Then, choose a creature to \"cipher\" the spell onto. Whenever that creature deals damage to an opponent, you may cast the \"ciphered\" spell without paying its cost. Sounds really strong, but usu"
  Connive,keyword,Ledger Shredder,"Written as \"[CARDNAME] connives\" Whenever a card connives, you draw and discard a card. If a nonland card was discarded this way, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature that connived."
  Conspire,keyword,Giantbaiting,"Only on instants and sorceries. When you cast a spell with conspire, you may tap 2 creatures that share a color with the spell. If you do, copy that spell."
  Convoke,keyword,March of the Multitudes,"Convoke allows you to tap creatures to pay for the cost in a spell. Creatures tapped with convoke can either pay for generic costs or colored costs, as long as they are the same color as the mana symbol they are paying."
  Coven,keyword,Augur of Autumn,"If you control at least 3 creatures with different powers, then creatures with coven gain some benefit."
  Crew,keyword,Aethersphere Harvester,"Written as \"Crew X\" where X is a number Only on vehicles. To crew a vehicle, you must tap any number of creatures whos power equals X or greater."
  Cumulative Upkeep,keyword,Mystic Remora,"Written as \"Cumulative Upkeep [cost]\" Old and difficult mechanic. Essentially, the cost compounds each turn, and must be paid at the upkeep step. On your upkeep you place an age-counter on the card with cumulative upkeep, then pay the upkeep cost as many times"
  Cycling,keyword,Cast Out,"Written as \"Cycling [cost] Whenever a card has cycling, you may pay the cycling cost and discard that card. Then you draw a new card."
  Dash,keyword,"Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer","You may pay the dash cost for a creature, that creature gains haste and returns to your hand at the end of the turn. Helps you dodge sorcery speed removal spells, like board sweepers."
  Daybound/Nightbound,keyword,Brutal Cathar,"The day/night cycle must be introduced by a card with daybound/nightbound. Whenever a player plays 2 or more spells on their turn, it becomes day. If a player casts no spells during their turn, it becomes night. Cards with this mechanic transform or give some"
  Delve,keyword,Treasure Cruise,"Delve allows you to exile cards from your graveyard to pay the generic mana cost of the card with delve. For example, with Treasure Cruise if you have 12 cards in your graveyard, you may pay 1 blue mana and \"delve\" 7 cards to draw 3 cards while only paying 1 m"
  Detain,keyword,Lavinia of the Tenth,"Whenever a player \"detains\" a permanent, that permanent cannot attack, block, or activate abilities until the start of that player's next turn."
  Devour,keyword,Predator Dragon,"Written as \"Devour X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with devour enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice any number of creatures you control. The creature with devour then gets X +1/+1 counters for each creature sacrificed this way."
  Disturb,keyword,Lunarch Veteran,"Written as \"Disturb [cost]\" Whenever a card with disturb is in your graveyard, you may cast it for its disturb cost. When you do, it enters the battlefield transformed."
  Dredge,keyword,Life from the Loam,"Written as \"Dredge X\", where X is a number If a card with dredge is in your graveyard, instead of drawing a card, you may put the top X cards of your library into your graveyard where X number associated with the ability, and return the dredge card to your han"
  Echo,keyword,Avalanche Riders,"Written as \"Echo [cost]\" Whenever a card with echo comes into play under your control, you must pay the echo cost at the beginning of the next upkeep or sacrifice the creature."
  Embalm,keyword,Aven Wind Guide,"Written as \"Embalm [cost]\" When a creature is in the graveyard, you may pay the embalm cost to exile that creature from your graveyard and make a token of it."
  Emerge,keyword,"",Emerge allows you to sacrifice a creature and pay the difference between the sacrificed creature's mana cost and the emerge cost. Very similar to offering mechanic in that way.
  Entwine,keyword,Tooth and Nail,"Written as \"Entwine [cost]\" On cards with 2 options, it allows you to pay mana in addition to the casting cost to do both options."
  Epic,keyword,Enduring Ideal,"After a card with Epic resolves, you may no longer cast spells. Instead, it provides you with (typically), some insane benefit."
  Escape,keyword,Cling to Dust,"Written as \"Escape [cost]\" You may cast a card from the graveyard for it's escape cost by exiling a specified amount of other cards from your graveyard."
  Evoke,keyword,Mulldrifter,"You may cast a card for its evoke cost, but when it enters the battlefield, it is immediately sacrificed. The evoke cost is usually much less than the cost of casting the card."
  Evolve,keyword,Experiment One,"Whenever a creature with power or toughness greater than a creature with evolve enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on the creature with evolve. If you play Experiment One on turn 1, then Watchwolf on turn 2, Experiment One will have a +1/+1 counter pu"
  Exalted,keyword,Noble Hierarch,"Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gets +1/+1 for each instance of exalted. If you have 2 creatures with exalted, and one of them attacks alone, that is 2 instances of exalted, so that creatures ends up getting +2/+2."
  Exert,keyword,Glorybringer,"When a creature with exert attacks, you may \"exert\" the card. If you do, it does not untap during its controller's next untap step. Cards grant some ability when you exert them."
  Exploit,keyword,Fell Stinger,"Whenever you cast a card with exploit, as an additional cost, you may sacrifice a creature. If you do, you gain some benefit."
  Explore,keyword,Merfolk Branchwalker,"Whenever a creature with explore enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it is a land card, put it into your hand. If it is a nonland card, you may put it into your graveyard. For each nonland card revealed this way, put a +1/+1 counter"
  Extort,keyword,Blind Obedience,"Whenever you cast a spell you may pay either white or black mana. If you do, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain life equal to the amount of life lost this way. Because the white mana symbol on extort cards is in the reminder text, extort cards can be play"
  Fabricated,keyword,Angel of Invention,"Written as \"Fabricate X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with fabricate enters the battlefield, you may either put X +1/+1 counters on that creature or create X 1/1 colorless servo creature tokens."
  Fading,keyword,Tangle Wire,"Written as \"Fading X\", where X is a number Cards with fading enter the battlefield with X fading counters on them. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a fading counter from that permanent. If you cannot remove a fading counter, sacrifice that creature."
  Fateseal,keyword,Spin into myth,"When you \"scry\" on your opponents' library. You are allowed to look at the top X cards of the opponent's library, as dictated by the number in the keyword. You then decide what stays on top of the library and what goes to the bottom."
  Fear,keyword,Dross Prowler,Only on black cards. The creature that has fear cannot be blocked except by black and artifact creatures.
  Flanking,keyword,Benalish Cavalry,"Whenever a creature with flanking is blocked, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until the end of the turn. Older mechanic; rare and not all that good."
  Flashback,keyword,Faithless Looting,"Written as \"Flashback [cost]\" When a card with flashback is in the graveyard, you may cast it for its flashback cost, then exile it."
  Flip,keyword,"Erayo, Soratami Ascendant","Flip cards are turned upside-down when a certain condition is met. They are not turned face-down, but rotated 180 degrees."
  Forecast,keyword,Proclamation of Rebirth,"Written as \"Forecast [cost]\" During your upkeep, you may pay the forecast cost and reveal the forecast card from your hand, then the ability from forecast resolves."
  Foretell,keyword,Doomskar,"Written as \"Foretell [cost]\" During your turn, at any time, you may pay 2 to \"foretell\" a card. You may cast that card for its foretell cost on a later turn."
  Frenzy,keyword,Frenzy Sliver,"Written as \"Frenzy X\" where X is a number Whenever a creature with frenzy attacks and isn't blocked, it gets +X/+0 until the end of turn."
  Graft,keyword,Plaxcaster Frogling,"Written as \"Graft X\" where X is a number All creatures with graft are 0/0s that enter the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on them equal to the graft number. Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, creatures with graft may move one of their counters"
  Gravestorm,keyword,Bitter Ordeal,"When the spell is cast, copy it for each permanent that entered the graveyard this turn. Only on one card with the mechanic."
  Haunt,keyword,Belfry Spirit,"Once a creature or spell with haunt enters the graveyard, it is exiled and then attached to a creature on the battlefield to \"haunt it\". All cards with the haunt mechanic have an enter the battlefield trigger that is the same as the haunt trigger. The haunt tr"
  Hideaway,keyword,Mosswort Bridge,"When a card with hideaway enters the battlefield, you look at the top 4 cards of your library. Exile one card under the hideaway permanent. Then, when a condition is met, you cast the exiled card without paying its mana cost. Only on 5 cards from a set called"
  Horsemanship,keyword,"Sun Quan, Lord of Wu","Horsemanship is like flying. Creatures with horsemanship can't be blocked by creatures without horsemanship, unless explicitly stated otherwise. Only from an old set called Portal: 3 Kingdoms. Set in the 3 Kingdoms era in China. Was originally meant to try to"
  Imprint,keyword,Extraplanar Lens,"Written as \"Imprint [something]\" When a card with imprint enters the battlefield, it can have you exile almost anything, then gives you some boon based on that."
  Indestructible,keyword,"Avacyn, Angle of Hope","Creatures with indestructible cannot be removed from the battlefield by effects that say \"destroy\" nor damage. You can remove indestructible creatures and permanents by exile effects (Swords to Plowshares), -1/-1 effects (Toxic Deluge), and bounce effects (Cyc"
  Inspired,keyword,"King Macar, the Gold-Cursed","Whenever a card with inspired becomes untapped, something happens."
  Investigate,keyword,Thraben Inspector,"Whenever a card investigates, create a clue tokens. Clue tokens have \"Pay 2 mana and sacrifice this artifact, draw a card.\""
  Jump-start,keyword,Radical Idea,Cards with Jump-start may be cast from the graveyard by paying their mana cost and discarding a card.
  Kicker,keyword,"Tourach, Dread Cantor","Written as \"Kicker [cost]\" When you cast a spell, you may also pay the kicker cost to have an additional effect happen."
  Level up,keyword,Lighthouse Chronologist,"Cards with level up enter the battlefield at level 0. You may pay the level up cost to put a level counter on that creature. As creatures \"gain experience (level up)\", they gain more abilities. You may only level up as a sorcery, but may do so as many times as"
  Landwalk,keyword,Benthic Behemoth,"Written as \"plainswalk\" or \"islandwalk\",etc Creatures with landwalk cannot be blocked if the defending player has a land that is the type mentioned in the ability."
  Living Weapon,keyword,Batterskull,"Cards with living weapon are equipment. When they enter the battlefield, they generate a 0/0 black germ creature token, and attach themselves to that creature. Since the germs have no abilities and are 0/0 creatures, they will die if the equipment becomes unat"
  Madness,keyword,Basking Rootwalla,"Written as \"Madness [cost]\" When a spell with madness is discarded, it is exiled. Then, you may cast that card for it's madness cost. If you don't cast it, it is then moved to the graveyard."
  Manifest,keyword,Reality Shift,"Written as \"Manifest [one or more cards]\" Manifested cards are face-down 2/2 creatures, just like morphs. Manifested creatures may be turned face up for their mana cost."
  Meld,keyword,"Brisela, Voice of Nightmares","2 cards can be melded together to create a single creature. Only in one set, not many cards."
  Mentor,keyword,Legion Warboss,"Whenever a card with mentor attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target attacking creature with less power than the mentor creature. If for some reason, a mentor card is put into the battlefield attacking, it does not trigger mentor. The act of declaring it as an a"
  Miracle,keyword,Temporal Mastery,"You may cast a card for its miracle cost if it is the first card you draw in a turn. Since the timing on miracles is different, if you draw a sorcery on an opponent's turn and it has miracle, you may cast it for its miracle cost, even though it is a sorcery."
  Modular,keyword,Arcbound Mouser,"Written as \"Modular X\", where X is a number Creatures with modular enter with X +1/+1 counters. When a creature with modular dies, it's counters may be moved to another target artifact creature."
  Monstrosity,keyword,Fleecemane Lion,"Written as \"[cost]: Monstrosity X\", where X is a number As long as a card has not already become monstrous, you may pay the monstrosity cost and put X +1/+1 counters on that creature."
  Morph and Megamorph,keyword,Ainok Survivalist,"Written as \"Morph [cost]\" You may pay 3 generic mana and put a card with morph onto the battlefield face down as a colorless 2/2 creature. Then you may pay the morph cost to flip the card face up."
  Mutate,keyword,Dirge Bat,"Written as \"Mutate [cost]\" Creatures may be cast for their mutate cost if targeting a non-human creature you control to mutate onto."
  Ninjutsu,keyword,Ninja of the Deep Hours,"Written as \"Ninjutsu [cost]\" You may return an unblocked attacking creature you control and put a ninja down in its' place, attacking."
  Offering,keyword,Patron of the Kitsune,"Written as \"[creature type] offering\" Creatures with offering may be cast as though it has flash if you sacrifice a creature of the appropriate type. Also, the mana cost is altered based on what you sacrifice. For example, Patron of the Orochi has snake offeri"
  Overload,keyword,Vandalblast,"Written as \"Overload [cost]\" When an instant or sorcery is overloaded, instead of targeting 1 target, it affects all targets."
  Persist,keyword,Kitchen Finks,"If a creature with persist is put into a graveyard from play and had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter. Doubles up enter the battlefield triggers and death triggers and stuff."
  Phasing,keyword,Sandbar Crocodile,"Old and complicated mechanic Cards that are phased out are treated as though they don't exist. Any auras and equipment attached do not fall off and are phased out with the creature. It's similar to exile, but the creatures return at the beginning of their cont"
  Poisonous,keyword,Virulent Sliver,"Written as \"Poisonous X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with poisonous deals damage to a player, that player gets X poison counters, where X is the number associated with the ability. If a player has 10 poison counters, they lose the game."
  Populate,keyword,Growing Ranks,Make a copy of a creature token you control.
  Proliferate,keyword,Grateful Apparition,"Whenever you proliferate, you may add an additional counter to anything that already has a counter. This includes +1/+1 counters, loyalty counters, poison counters, etc. Basically all counters."
  Provoke,keyword,Lowland Tracker,"When a creature with provoke attacks, its controller may target a creature defending player controls. Then, untap that creature (if applicable). That creature must block the attacking creature with provoke. They mostly suck in general."
  Prowl,keyword,Latchkey Faerie,"Written as \"Prowl [cost]\" A creature may be cast for its prowl cost, only if a creature that shares a creature type dealt damage to a player this turn."
  Rampage,keyword,Craw Giant,"Written as \"Rampage X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with rampage is blocked, it gets +X/+X until end of turn for each creature blocking it."
  Rebound,keyword,Ephemerate,"Whenever you cast a card with rebound, exile it. You may cast that card again without paying its mana cost on your next upkeep."
  Recover,keyword,Icefall,"Written as \"Recover [cost]\" Whenever a creature is put into a player's graveyard from the battlefield, all cards with recover trigger. You may then pay the recover cost for each card and return it to your hand. If you do not or cannot pay the cost, the card is"
  Reinforce,keyword,Burrenton Bombardier,"Written as \"Reinforce: X - [cost]\", where X is a number You may discard a card with reinforce from your hand and pay the reinforce cost, then put X +1/+1 counters on target creature"
  Renown,keyword,Scab-Clan Berserker,"Written as \"Reinforce X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with renown deals combat damage to a player for the first time, put X +1/+1 counters on it. It then becomes renown."
  Replicate,keyword,Shattering Spree,"Written as \"Replicate [cost]\" Whenever you cast a spell, you may pay its replicate cost any number of times. If you do, copy that spell for each time you paid the replicate cost."
  Retrace,keyword,Oona's Grace,"Cards with retrace may be cast from the graveyard if you discard a land card in addition to paying their other costs. Unlike most other versions of this, they are not exiled once cast from the graveyard, so you can keep retracing them as long as you have lands"
  Riot,keyword,Gruul Spellbreaker,"Whenever a creature with riot enters the battlefield, its controller chooses for it to enter with either a +1/+1 counter and haste."
  Ripple,keyword,Surging Dementia,"Written as \"Ripple X\", where X is a number When a spell is cast with Ripple, its controller may reveal the top X cards of their library and cast any copies of that card without paying the mana cost. This triggers ripple again."
  Scavenge,keyword,Deadbridge Goliath,"Written as \"Scavenge [cost]\" You may exile a card with scavenge from your graveyard by paying it's scavenge cost. Then, place a number of +1/+1 counters on target creature."
  Shadow,keyword,Dauthi Cutthroat,Creatures with shadow can only block or be blocked by other creatures with shadow.
  Shroud,keyword,Argothian Enchantress,Creatures with shroud cannot be the target of spells or abilities. That includes all players.
  Soulbond,keyword,Deadeye Navigator,Creatures with souldbond enter the battlefield and bond to another creature. Both creatures then gain some boon.
  Soulshift,keyword,Elder Pine of Jukai,"Written as \"Soulshift X\", where X is a number Whenever a creature with soulshift is put into the graveyard, its controller may return a spirit card from the graveyard to their hand with mana value X or less."
  Spectacle,keyword,Light up the Stage,"Written as \"Spectacle [cost]\" You may cast a card for its spectacle cost if an opponent was dealt damage this turn."
  Splice,keyword,Everdream,"Written as \"Splice onto X\", where X is a card type When you cast a card of the specified type, you may pay the splice cost and reveal that card. The effect of the revealed card is then \"tacked onto\" the spell being cast."
  Split Second,keyword,Angel's Grace,"A card with split second cannot be interacted with. Once it is on the stack, nothing else can be put there until it has resolved."
  Storm,keyword,Grapeshot,"Whenever a card with storm is cast, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. For example, if you cast 2 lightning bolts and then a Grapeshot, there are actually 3 copies of grapeshot because it is copied 2 times from the 2 lightning bolts cast before i"
  Sunburst,keyword,Engineered Explosives,"A card with sunburst enters with a counter on it for each color of mana used to cast the spell. If a card with sunburst cost 5 generic mana, and you spend 3 green mana and 2 black mana, it only gets 2 counters. If you spend one of every color of mana, it gets"
  Support,keyword,Generous Patron,"Written as \"Support X\", where X is a number When the ability resolves, place a +1/+1 counter on up to X target creatures."
  Surveil,keyword,Notion Rain,"Written as \"Surveil X\", where X is a number When the ability resolves, look at the top X cards of your library. You may put any number into your graveyard and rest back on top of your library in any order."
  Suspend,keyword,Rift Bolt,"Written as \"Suspend X [cost]\", where X is a number You may pay the suspend cost for a card and exile it with X time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from the card. When the last time counter is removed, you may then cast t"
  Totem Armor,keyword,Bear Umbra,"Totem Armor is only on auras. If a creature attached with an aura that has Totem Armor would die, instead, the aura is destroyed instead."
  Transfigure,keyword,Fleshwrither,"Written as \"Transfigure [cost]\" Any time a sorcery could be cast, you may pay the transfigure cost and sacrifice the creature with transfigure to search your library for a creature with the same mana value."
  Transform,keyword,Aberrant Researcher // Perfected Form,"Applies to double-faced cards. When some condition is met, you may transform a card from its front side to its back side. What causes a transformation varies widely from in-game actions to mana costs."
  Transmute,keyword,Muddle the Mixture,"Written as \"Transmute [cost]\" When you transmute a card, you pay the transmute cost and discard that card, then search your library for a card with the same mana value."
  Tribute,keyword,Fanatic of Xenagos,"Written as \"Tribute X\", where X is a number. Whenever a creature with tribute enters the battlefield, an opponent may pay \"tribute\" by putting X +1/+1 counters on it. If the tribute is not paid, some other effect will occur."
  Undying,keyword,Young Wolf,"When a creature with undying is put into the graveyard, if it had no +1/+1 counters, return it to the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter. Yes, this is persist with +1 counters instead of -1 counters."
  Unearth,keyword,Dregscape Zombie,"Written as \"Unearth [cost]\" When a creature with unearth is in the graveyard, you may pay the unearth cost any time you could play a sorcery. Return that creature to the battlefield, and it gains haste. Exile it at the end step."
  Unleash,keyword,Rakdos Cackler,"When a creature with unleash enters the battlefield, its controller may choose to have it enter with a +1/+1 counter on it. If a creature with unleash has a counter on it, it cannot block. The counter does not have to come from unleash, it's any +1/+1 counter."
  Wither,keyword,Harvest Gwyllion,"Wither is a replacement effect. If a creature would be dealt nonlethal damage by a creature with wither, it instead has -1/-1 counters placed on it instead of marking normal damage. This is similar to infect, but players do not receive poison counters from cre"
  Addendum,ability_word,Emergency Powers,Cards with addendum have an added effect if cast in your main phase.
  Battalion,ability_word,Legion Loyalist,Creatures with battalion have an additional effect trigger if they attack with at least 2 other creatures
  Chroma,ability_word,Fiery Bombardment,"Cards with chroma check for specific mana symbols in specific zones, then give a benefit or effect based on that."
  Domain,ability_word,Prismatic Geoscope,"Cards with domain have some effect related to the number of basic land types you control. Some good effects, some bad effects."
  Enrage,ability_word,Ranging Raptors,"Only on creatures. If a creature with enrage is dealt damage, some type of trigger will occur."
  Fateful Hour,ability_word,Break of Day,Cards with fateful hour gain an additional ability if it's controller is at 5 or less life.
  Ferocious,ability_word,Wild Slash,Cards with ferocious gain an additional ability if their controller also controls a creature with more than 4 power.
  Grandeur,ability_word,"Baru, Fist of Krosa",Very few cards with this and they are bad. Allows you to discard a card with the same name to give it a bonus.
  Hellbent,ability_word,Infernal Tutor,"Cards with hellbent give some additional boon or greater effect if you have no cards in hand when the card resolves. If you cast the card, and while it is on the stack, you somehow discard your hand, you will still get the hellbent ability even though you had"
  Heroic,ability_word,Fabled Hero,Cards with heroic grant some additional benefit when targeted with a spell.
  Join forces,ability_word,Collective Voyage,Cards with join forces allow all players to contribute mana towards some effect. Meant for commander/multiplayer games.
  Kinship,ability_word,Pyroclast Consul,"On your upkeep, if you control a card with kinship, you may look at the top card of your library. If it is a creature that shares a type with the kinship creature on the battlefield, you may reveal it for some effect."
  Landfall,ability_word,Khalni Heart Expedition,Cards with landfall have some ability that triggers when a land enters the battlefield.
  Metalcraft,ability_word,Puresteel Paladin,Cards with metalcraft gain an additional benefit if it's controller controls 3 or more artifacts.
  Morbid,ability_word,Tragic Slip,Cards with morbid gain some effect if a creature died that turn.
  Radiance,ability_word,Rally the Righteous,"Basically, if you target a permanent with a spell, that spell affects all permanents of the same type that share a color. If you have 5 white creatures and cast Rally the Righteous on one, the other 4 with also get +3/+3"
  Raid,ability_word,Bloodsoaked Champion,Cards with raid get some effect if their controller attacked before playing them.
  Rally,ability_word,Lantern Scout,Cards with rally have some effect trigger whenever a creature with the type Ally enters the battlefield.
  Sweep,ability_word,Charge Across the Araba,"When you cast a spell with sweep, you may return any number of lands with the basic land type as dictated by the card. Some effect is gained from this. Not a good mechanic."
  Threshold,ability_word,Nimble Mongoose,Cards with threshold gain some effect when you have 7 or more cards in the graveyard.
  Undergrowth,ability_word,Kraul Foragers,Cards with undergrowth have effects dependent on the amount of creatures in your graveyard.
